    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_5536072d49a78931c4d10667a07d190d226ccf1370800641b980a2c9632fb8eb",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source exposes a verification tradeoff between two ways of obtaining c_k. Direct evaluation of the defining binomial sum is independent of RH but is badly conditioned, with a source-reported working-precision heuristic growing as k log10(2). The trend-plus-zero decomposition and its critical-line wave approximation make very large indices tractable, but the zero formula assumes simple zeros and the wave form additionally assumes RH; agreement with direct values therefore checks the approximation over the compared range without independently validating those assumptions.",
