    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_a164bb82c3518d889a0a951c5f8e16844570cc77dcf32572a9529ed91ba8ebfc",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The discrete Baez-Duarte criterion and the continuous Riesz criterion are connected by an exact exponential generating identity: once c_0 is included, the generating series of the finite-difference sequence is e^xR(x)/x. The cited coefficient-growth equivalence then shifts an exponent delta for c_k to delta+1 for R(x), so the RH-scale decay k^{-3/4+epsilon} and growth x^{1/4+epsilon} are two representations of the same asymptotic condition.",
